      ],
      "radius": 1.6,
      "prompt": "Press E — Living room",
      "srHint": "The living room fills the northwest quadrant.",
      "trigger": {
        "type": "prose",
        "text": "LIVING ROOM (NW quadrant, the biggest room): couch against the WEST wall; comfortable chair north-central by the window; ottoman south of the centre rug; windows on the north and west walls; photo shelf on the west wall behind the couch."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "room-kitchen",
      "label": "Kitchen",
      "mode": "prompted",
      "shape": "radius",
      "position": [
        7.2,
        0,
        -6.7
      ],
      "radius": 1.3,
      "prompt": "Press E — Kitchen",
      "srHint": "The kitchen is the small northeast room, behind the peninsula.",
      "trigger": {
        "type": "prose",
        "text": "KITCHEN (NE quadrant, visibly the SMALL room): L-counter along the north wall (sink under the window) and east wall (stove at the north end, fridge immediately south — tight work triangle, v3.1). The PENINSULA closes the west side: attached at its north end, ONE-PIECE countertop, four stools on its living-room side, dishwasher on its kitchen side."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "room-hallway",
      "label": "Interior hallway",
      "mode": "prompted",
      "shape": "radius",
      "position": [
        5.55,
        0,
        -2.7
      ],
      "radius": 0.9,
      "prompt": "Press E — Hallway",
      "srHint": "The interior hallway runs north from the entry door to the open living space.",
      "trigger": {
        "type": "prose",
        "text": "INTERIOR HALLWAY: entry door at the south end, opening north into the living/kitchen space — Mal’s sight-line to the kitchen. One small hall-closet door on the west side, directly opposite the laundry door; bath door and laundry-closet door on the east side. The techs carry the tank through here and out the door."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "room-bedroom",
      "label": "Bedroom",
      "mode": "prompted",
      "shape": "radius",
      "position": [
        2,
        0,
        -1.8
      ],
      "radius": 1.5,
      "prompt": "Press E — Bedroom",
      "srHint": "The bedroom fills the southwest quadrant.",
      "trigger": {
        "type": "prose",
        "text": "BEDROOM (SW quadrant): bed, west-wall window. Bedroom closet on its east side with TWO BIG DOORS. The small hall closet sits at the closet column’s north end (door on the hallway side, opposite the laundry). Person-door: from the living room (north wall), opening inward against the closet wall. The old entry-alcove door is gone — the alcove is sealed (Rebecca 2026-08-20)."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "room-bath",
      "label": "Bathroom",
      "mode": "prompted",
      "shape": "radius",
      "position": [
        7.4,
